WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.188
Question two.

00:00:01.188 --> 00:00:07.312
Step one: macro scan. It asks which model the whole flow best fits.

00:00:07.312 --> 00:00:10.694
One mark. Command words: “best fits”.

00:00:10.694 --> 00:00:12.339
Step two: denoise.

00:00:12.339 --> 00:00:17.000
Useful, in yellow: collect ballots, tally, display.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:19.377
In cyan: “the whole flow”.

00:00:19.377 --> 00:00:24.769
Useless red herring: class election, tablets — kick it out.

00:00:24.769 --> 00:00:26.415
Step three: draft.

00:00:26.415 --> 00:00:28.517
Collect ballots: input.

00:00:28.517 --> 00:00:29.888
Tally: process.

00:00:29.888 --> 00:00:31.350
Display: output.

00:00:31.350 --> 00:00:32.904
Step four: P O E.

00:00:32.904 --> 00:00:37.748
A, store, output, input: wrong order and names — cut.

00:00:37.748 --> 00:00:43.963
C, compress, transmit, decompress: no compression in the stem — cut.

00:00:43.963 --> 00:00:49.630
D, encrypt, back up, restore: no encryption in the stem — cut.

00:00:49.630 --> 00:00:59.044
Step five: sanity check and lock. Input, process, output — three steps match three actions, same order.

00:00:59.044 --> 00:01:01.512
So the correct answer is B.
